  "implemented": [
    "CharacterController consumes prepared reaction frames, binds the current shared event track, projects ordered outgoing/current samples with native weights/ease and recovers inactive actions at the following actor prefix.",
    "Contact dispatch can replace a strike after its actor input prefix. The same tail binds the new reaction. Outgoing layers alongside a strike use its already advanced clock, with no second duration increment.",
    "Background samples borrow existing shared animation clocks so runAnimation advances them before pose sampling; current/outgoing owned samples retain explicit service times. Current reaction traversal emits its own keys, while private outgoing samples traverse no event track.",
    "BlockHit uses a distinct shared priority to keep BlockIdle resident. Recoil/Stagger remove cached BlockIdle. Existing interruption paths clear typed reaction/outgoing ownership and private projection without inventing ownership for legacy raw actions.",
    "Model/view restoration can clear shared animation state while a render ID survives. Reaction and strike binding shortcuts now require the actual shared track to be present and rebind from durable time when absent.",
    "A transition log records actual actor-prefix recovery. Continuation scenarios await that event, then independently inspect saved state rather than using wall-clock delay as completion proof."
  ],
